1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,190
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,190 --> 00:00:04,390
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,390 --> 00:00:05,610
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,160 --> 00:00:07,180
I've been an ER nurse

5
00:00:07,180 --> 00:00:08,320
for thirty years.

6
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:09,690
Running up and down those
halls

7
00:00:09,690 --> 00:00:11,210
for twelve hours a shift.

8
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:12,150
I had my right knee

9
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:13,890
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:15,980
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:16,670 --> 00:00:18,040
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:19,660
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:20,740
and it went away.

14
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:22,260
This is different.

15
00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:23,200
Tight.

16
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:24,080
Full.

17
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:25,010
Like a band around

18
00:00:25,010 --> 00:00:26,700
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:27,870
And for two years I've

20
00:00:27,870 --> 00:00:29,280
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:30,480
Give it time.

22
00:00:30,610 --> 00:00:32,350
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:32,350 --> 00:00:33,750
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:34,470 --> 00:00:35,370
At three months,

25
00:00:35,370 --> 00:00:36,300
give it six.

26
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:37,420
At six months,

27
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:39,000
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:39,870
At a year,

29
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:41,730
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:41,870 --> 00:00:43,010
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:44,300
We went down the list.

32
00:00:44,340 --> 00:00:45,740
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:45,780 --> 00:00:47,120
Every session,

34
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:48,990
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:50,800
I got stronger.

36
00:00:50,850 --> 00:00:52,590
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:52,650 --> 00:00:53,950
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:53,950 --> 00:00:55,190
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:57,420
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:57,420 --> 00:00:58,550
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:58,550 --> 00:01:00,150
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:01,990
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:03,840
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:04,010 --> 00:01:05,570
And after that, a second

45
00:01:05,570 --> 00:01:06,860
operation to go back

46
00:01:06,860 --> 00:01:08,330
in and do it over.

47
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:09,990
I said no.

48
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:12,660
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

49
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:13,650
and my knee felt like

50
00:01:13,650 --> 00:01:15,360
a band was wrapped around
it,

51
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:18,020
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

52
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:19,600
Every morning I took
something

53
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:21,400
for it and went to my
shift.

54
00:01:22,270 --> 00:01:23,600
Couldn't do the stairs,

55
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:24,700
couldn't stand at the
counter

56
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:26,240
long enough to finish
dinner,

57
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:27,960
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

58
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:30,200
without shifting every two
minutes.

59
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:31,070
At work

60
00:01:31,070 --> 00:01:32,820
I'd duck into the supply
room

61
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:34,420
just to sit down for a
minute.

62
00:01:34,950 --> 00:01:36,230
One busy night,

63
00:01:36,230 --> 00:01:38,130
a patient's daughter asked
if I needed

64
00:01:38,130 --> 00:01:40,270
the wheelchair more than
her mom did.

65
00:01:40,310 --> 00:01:41,760
It woke me at night,

66
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:43,880
and it turned ordinary
things,

67
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:44,860
like getting in the car

68
00:01:44,860 --> 00:01:46,580
after a shift

69
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:47,960
or up off the couch,

70
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:49,180
into a decision.

71
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:50,520
After a long and serious

72
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:51,780
talk with my husband,

73
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:53,690
I went back in one more
time.

74
00:01:53,890 --> 00:01:54,840
That was the fourth set

75
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:56,340
of X-rays on this knee.

76
00:01:57,030 --> 00:01:58,530
And like the three before
it,

77
00:01:58,530 --> 00:02:01,110
the answer was everything
looks great.

78
00:02:01,150 --> 00:02:03,280
No loosening, no
infection,

79
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:04,290
nothing wrong.

80
00:02:04,330 --> 00:02:05,420
Only this time

81
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:06,830
there was no new number.

82
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:09,570
Nobody said give it
another six months.

83
00:02:09,610 --> 00:02:11,510
There was nothing left to
give it.

84
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:12,660
I sat in the parking

85
00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:13,750
lot for a while.

86
00:02:14,010 --> 00:02:15,430
Okay, I thought.

87
00:02:15,510 --> 00:02:16,880
Then explain this.

88
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,240
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

89
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,780
I hit my breaking point.

90
00:02:20,870 --> 00:02:23,000
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

91
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:25,260
I'd worked a twelve-hour
shift that day.

92
00:02:25,430 --> 00:02:27,310
Everyone in the house was
asleep

93
00:02:27,310 --> 00:02:28,870
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

94
00:02:28,870 --> 00:02:29,940
with my leg up,

95
00:02:29,940 --> 00:02:31,520
trying to find any angle
where

96
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:32,550
it didn't feel like
something

97
00:02:32,550 --> 00:02:34,650
was wrapped around my knee
and tightening.

98
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:37,010
My husband didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

99
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:39,220
By then I'd stopped
telling him.

100
00:02:39,830 --> 00:02:40,920
And I just thought,

101
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:42,520
is this really my life
now?

102
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:43,990
I can't live like this.

103
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:45,470
Thirty years of taking
care

104
00:02:45,470 --> 00:02:46,620
of everybody else,

105
00:02:46,620 --> 00:02:47,450
and I couldn't take care

106
00:02:47,450 --> 00:02:48,390
of my own knee.

107
00:02:48,590 --> 00:02:50,290
So I made myself a
promise.

108
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:51,290
I wouldn't go a day

109
00:02:51,290 --> 00:02:52,820
without looking for an
answer.

110
00:02:53,030 --> 00:02:54,460
And when I found one,

111
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:55,590
I'd share it with everyone

112
00:02:55,590 --> 00:02:57,020
going through the same
thing.

113
00:02:57,230 --> 00:02:58,410
So I got my laptop

114
00:02:58,410 --> 00:02:59,760
out and went looking.

115
00:02:59,990 --> 00:03:01,130
Not for a product.

116
00:03:01,170 --> 00:03:02,510
For an explanation.

117
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:04,870
Mayo Clinic forums,

118
00:03:04,870 --> 00:03:06,940
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

119
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:09,710
doctor videos, medical
animations.

120
00:03:09,810 --> 00:03:11,540
And that's when I found a
video

121
00:03:11,540 --> 00:03:13,780
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

122
00:03:13,820 --> 00:03:15,960
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

123
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:17,840
had been through exactly
this.

124
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:19,760
But before I say anything
else,

125
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:21,360
I want to be straight with
you.

126
00:03:22,050 --> 00:03:24,210
You've already had
something work fast.

127
00:03:24,250 --> 00:03:24,960
The ice.

128
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:26,690
The first week of a new
pill.

129
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:28,520
The good day after a
session.

130
00:03:28,670 --> 00:03:29,770
Then it wore off.

131
00:03:29,850 --> 00:03:31,790
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

132
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:33,710
Fast relief isn't relief.

133
00:03:33,770 --> 00:03:34,770
It's a preview.

134
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:36,150
So I'm not going to tell

135
00:03:36,150 --> 00:03:37,440
you this works fast.

136
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:38,340
It doesn't.

137
00:03:38,770 --> 00:03:40,460
But if you're willing to
be patient,

138
00:03:40,460 --> 00:03:41,220
and to look at what's

139
00:03:41,220 --> 00:03:42,870
going on around your new
knee

140
00:03:42,870 --> 00:03:44,330
instead of inside it,
there

141
00:03:44,330 --> 00:03:46,430
is a real reason it still
hurts.

142
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,360
And something you can do
about it.

143
00:03:49,290 --> 00:03:50,800
Let me explain what he
said,

144
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:52,400
because this is what
changed

145
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:53,370
everything for me.

146
00:03:53,410 --> 00:03:55,180
He started with the
basics.

147
00:03:55,220 --> 00:03:56,740
A knee replacement takes
out

148
00:03:56,740 --> 00:03:58,430
the worn joint surfaces

149
00:03:58,430 --> 00:04:00,400
and puts in metal and
plastic.

150
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:02,100
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

151
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:03,760
you had before the
operation.

152
00:04:03,980 --> 00:04:05,540
That part I already knew.

153
00:04:05,690 --> 00:04:07,000
But then he explained
something

154
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,530
nobody had ever told me.

155
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:09,600
He said,

156
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:10,770
think about a swollen foot

157
00:04:10,770 --> 00:04:11,900
inside a shoe.

158
00:04:11,970 --> 00:04:13,300
The shoe didn't shrink.

159
00:04:13,390 --> 00:04:15,370
Your foot is taking up
more room,

160
00:04:15,370 --> 00:04:16,940
so everything feels
cramped

161
00:04:16,940 --> 00:04:18,540
and tight and squeezed.

162
00:04:18,810 --> 00:04:19,850
Your new knee sits

163
00:04:19,850 --> 00:04:21,130
in a limited space

164
00:04:21,130 --> 00:04:23,380
with living tissue packed
all around it.

165
00:04:24,350 --> 00:04:26,140
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

166
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:27,840
had to work through that
tissue.

167
00:04:27,890 --> 00:04:30,440
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

168
00:04:30,510 --> 00:04:31,950
At first that's normal.

169
00:04:32,090 --> 00:04:33,380
But in some people

170
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:34,830
that swelling can stay
switched

171
00:04:34,830 --> 00:04:36,830
on far longer than
expected.

172
00:04:36,870 --> 00:04:38,570
And swollen tissue takes
up more

173
00:04:38,570 --> 00:04:40,280
room than calm tissue
does.

174
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:42,090
So when you bend,

175
00:04:42,090 --> 00:04:43,770
that tissue gets
compressed.

176
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:44,990
When you straighten,

177
00:04:44,990 --> 00:04:46,360
it gets pulled tight.

178
00:04:46,510 --> 00:04:47,630
That's the band.

179
00:04:47,670 --> 00:04:49,940
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

180
00:04:49,990 --> 00:04:50,770
And you start being

181
00:04:50,770 --> 00:04:51,900
the one who says,

182
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:52,760
you go ahead.

183
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:53,770
I'll stay here.

184
00:04:53,910 --> 00:04:55,560
And that's exactly why so
much

185
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:57,370
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

186
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:59,750
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

187
00:04:59,750 --> 00:05:00,700
around the knee.

188
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:01,790
Worth doing,

189
00:05:01,790 --> 00:05:02,860
and I'd done it.

190
00:05:02,930 --> 00:05:04,290
It does nothing about
tissue

191
00:05:04,290 --> 00:05:05,390
taking up room.

192
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:06,650
A nerve block quiets

193
00:05:06,650 --> 00:05:08,460
the nerve carrying the
signal.

194
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:10,620
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

195
00:05:11,270 --> 00:05:12,940
But when that irritated
tissue

196
00:05:12,940 --> 00:05:14,610
finally calms down,

197
00:05:14,610 --> 00:05:16,160
it holds less fluid,

198
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:17,870
and it takes up less room.

199
00:05:17,990 --> 00:05:19,560
Less room taken up means

200
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:21,520
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

201
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:23,410
That's what takes the
pressure off.

202
00:05:23,510 --> 00:05:25,120
After two years of this,

203
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:26,640
it finally made sense.

204
00:05:27,310 --> 00:05:29,170
The problem was never the
new knee.

205
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:31,180
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

206
00:05:31,220 --> 00:05:32,770
He calls it the squeeze.

207
00:05:32,810 --> 00:05:35,020
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

208
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:36,420
I'd bought knee sleeves,

209
00:05:36,420 --> 00:05:38,970
compression braces, good
nursing clogs,

210
00:05:38,970 --> 00:05:41,620
creams, half of Amazon
really,

211
00:05:41,620 --> 00:05:42,800
and all any of it gave

212
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:44,100
me was an hour.

213
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:45,130
I even looked at going

214
00:05:45,130 --> 00:05:47,180
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

215
00:05:47,290 --> 00:05:49,180
But at $200 a session

216
00:05:49,180 --> 00:05:50,960
with nothing covered by
insurance,

217
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:52,190
that was a quick no.

218
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:53,660
Then one night

219
00:05:53,660 --> 00:05:55,110
I went back to that knee
replacement

220
00:05:55,110 --> 00:05:56,650
group and actually read
it.

221
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:58,340
Thousands of people,

222
00:05:58,340 --> 00:05:59,990
years out from surgery,

223
00:05:59,990 --> 00:06:02,440
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

224
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:03,900
nobody could explain.

225
00:06:03,940 --> 00:06:05,860
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

226
00:06:05,860 --> 00:06:07,760
the same thing kept coming
up.

227
00:06:07,910 --> 00:06:09,230
This one device,

228
00:06:09,230 --> 00:06:11,230
and people saying it was
the first

229
00:06:11,230 --> 00:06:13,270
thing that made a
difference.

230
00:06:13,920 --> 00:06:16,150
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

231
00:06:16,150 --> 00:06:17,590
alright, here it comes,

232
00:06:17,590 --> 00:06:18,930
she's selling me
something,

233
00:06:18,930 --> 00:06:21,000
let me shut that down
right now.

234
00:06:21,110 --> 00:06:22,940
I'm only here because I
made myself

235
00:06:22,940 --> 00:06:25,120
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

236
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:26,150
that if I ever found

237
00:06:26,150 --> 00:06:27,390
something that helped,

238
00:06:27,390 --> 00:06:28,360
I'd say so.

239
00:06:28,730 --> 00:06:30,220
It's called the KenRelief

240
00:06:30,220 --> 00:06:31,740
Red Light Therapy Wrap.

241
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,050
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

242
00:06:34,130 --> 00:06:35,800
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

243
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:38,060
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

244
00:06:38,330 --> 00:06:40,460
But I went to their
website anyway,

245
00:06:40,460 --> 00:06:41,430
just to see what all

246
00:06:41,430 --> 00:06:42,690
the fuss was about.

247
00:06:42,790 --> 00:06:44,890
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

248
00:06:44,890 --> 00:06:47,410
charge $200 a session for,

249
00:06:47,410 --> 00:06:50,170
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

250
00:06:50,170 --> 00:06:51,090
in a wrap you plug

251
00:06:51,090 --> 00:06:52,360
into the wall at home.

252
00:06:52,550 --> 00:06:54,120
Two hundred and forty
lights.

253
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:56,080
Red at 660 nanometers

254
00:06:56,080 --> 00:06:58,270
and near-infrared at 850,

255
00:06:58,270 --> 00:07:00,320
run together for the
strongest effect.

256
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:02,120
Four strength levels.

257
00:07:02,190 --> 00:07:03,980
A five to thirty minute
timer.

258
00:07:04,140 --> 00:07:05,870
Then I saw the guarantee.

259
00:07:05,910 --> 00:07:07,130
Ninety days.

260
00:07:07,170 --> 00:07:09,000
Results or your money
back,

261
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,310
no questions, no store
credit,

262
00:07:11,310 --> 00:07:13,050
and you don't even send it
back.

263
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:15,470
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

264
00:07:15,470 --> 00:07:17,020
days to change my mind.

265
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:19,110
There wasn't much to lose,

266
00:07:19,110 --> 00:07:20,230
so I ordered it.

267
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:22,120
Two of them, actually.

268
00:07:22,270 --> 00:07:24,020
Only the right knee was
replaced,

269
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:26,120
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

270
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:27,180
and I'd done it every

271
00:07:27,180 --> 00:07:28,740
shift for two years.

272
00:07:29,040 --> 00:07:31,330
The left one was carrying
the difference.

273
00:07:31,370 --> 00:07:32,220
When it came,

274
00:07:32,220 --> 00:07:34,230
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

275
00:07:34,230 --> 00:07:35,290
because I'd been let down

276
00:07:35,290 --> 00:07:37,150
too many times to get
excited.

277
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:39,580
What I felt was warmth.

278
00:07:39,690 --> 00:07:41,680
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

279
00:07:41,910 --> 00:07:42,960
More like it was coming

280
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:44,330
from inside the knee

281
00:07:44,330 --> 00:07:45,730
and spreading around it.

282
00:07:46,170 --> 00:07:47,260
And that was it.

283
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:48,960
That was the whole
experience.

284
00:07:49,580 --> 00:07:50,800
When I took it off,

285
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:51,880
I'll be honest,

286
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:53,550
nothing dramatic had
happened.

287
00:07:53,870 --> 00:07:55,560
And after what that video
said,

288
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,350
that's exactly what I
expected.

289
00:07:57,390 --> 00:07:58,130
What was different

290
00:07:58,130 --> 00:07:58,960
was that for the first

291
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:00,220
time in two years

292
00:08:00,220 --> 00:08:01,810
I'd done something for my
knee

293
00:08:01,810 --> 00:08:02,820
instead of to it.

294
00:08:03,390 --> 00:08:04,330
Twenty minutes,

295
00:08:04,330 --> 00:08:05,330
in my own chair.

296
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:07,460
No drive, no copay.

297
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:08,790
They say twenty minutes.

298
00:08:08,830 --> 00:08:09,740
I did thirty,

299
00:08:09,740 --> 00:08:10,650
twice a day,

300
00:08:10,650 --> 00:08:12,320
lowest setting that first
week.

301
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:13,790
I wrote it on my schedule,

302
00:08:13,790 --> 00:08:15,190
right next to my shifts.

303
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:16,440
The first week,

304
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:17,210
I couldn't have told

305
00:08:17,210 --> 00:08:18,860
you if anything was
happening.

306
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:19,800
I tried not to get

307
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:20,680
my hopes up.

308
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:21,690
I'd had things help

309
00:08:21,690 --> 00:08:23,130
for a week and then stop.

310
00:08:23,170 --> 00:08:25,210
But somewhere in the
second week

311
00:08:25,210 --> 00:08:26,400
I noticed I'd come down

312
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:28,250
the stairs without holding
the rail.

313
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:30,250
I hadn't decided to.

314
00:08:30,290 --> 00:08:31,910
I just did it, then
stopped

315
00:08:31,910 --> 00:08:34,090
halfway down because I
realized.

316
00:08:34,230 --> 00:08:35,750
By the end of the fourth
week

317
00:08:35,750 --> 00:08:36,770
I'd slept through the
night

318
00:08:36,770 --> 00:08:38,070
four times running.

319
00:08:38,810 --> 00:08:39,990
I stood at the counter

320
00:08:39,990 --> 00:08:41,340
and finished making dinner

321
00:08:41,340 --> 00:08:42,880
without looking for the
stool.

322
00:08:42,970 --> 00:08:44,430
None of that is dramatic.

323
00:08:44,550 --> 00:08:45,460
All of it was gone

324
00:08:45,460 --> 00:08:46,560
for two years.

325
00:08:46,630 --> 00:08:48,160
A few weeks later my
husband asked

326
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:49,010
if I wanted to walk

327
00:08:49,010 --> 00:08:50,520
the long way around the
block.

328
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:51,710
And for the first time

329
00:08:51,710 --> 00:08:52,390
in two years,

330
00:08:52,390 --> 00:08:53,480
I said yes.

331
00:08:53,540 --> 00:08:54,880
I wanted to understand
why,

332
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:56,170
so I read the whole thing.

333
00:08:56,210 --> 00:08:57,850
It comes down to four
steps.

334
00:08:57,890 --> 00:08:58,550
One.

335
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:00,260
The tissue around a new
knee can

336
00:09:00,260 --> 00:09:02,990
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

337
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:03,850
Two.

338
00:09:03,890 --> 00:09:06,300
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

339
00:09:06,300 --> 00:09:07,110
so it takes up more

340
00:09:07,110 --> 00:09:08,200
room than it should.

341
00:09:08,300 --> 00:09:09,020
Three.

342
00:09:09,390 --> 00:09:11,150
There's only so much room
in there.

343
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,330
Bending compresses it.

344
00:09:13,380 --> 00:09:14,970
Straightening pulls it
tight.

345
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:16,910
That's the squeeze.

346
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:18,270
Four.

347
00:09:18,520 --> 00:09:20,470
Red and near-infrared
light have been

348
00:09:20,470 --> 00:09:22,790
studied for calming that
inflammation,

349
00:09:22,790 --> 00:09:24,210
so the swelling and the
pressure

350
00:09:24,210 --> 00:09:25,550
can come down with it.

351
00:09:25,670 --> 00:09:27,310
In a randomized trial,

352
00:09:27,310 --> 00:09:29,170
patients given light
therapy after

353
00:09:29,170 --> 00:09:30,360
a knee replacement

354
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:32,670
had less pain, less
swelling

355
00:09:32,670 --> 00:09:34,170
and better early movement

356
00:09:34,170 --> 00:09:35,420
than those who weren't.

357
00:09:35,460 --> 00:09:38,190
A 2025 review said the
same,

358
00:09:38,190 --> 00:09:39,520
and was clear the evidence

359
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:40,840
is still limited.

360
00:09:40,950 --> 00:09:42,520
I probably sound like a
broken

361
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:43,690
record to my family

362
00:09:43,690 --> 00:09:45,230
and everyone on my unit.

363
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:47,340
But after two years of
doing everything

364
00:09:47,340 --> 00:09:49,290
I was told and getting
nowhere,

365
00:09:49,290 --> 00:09:50,860
you have no idea what it's
like

366
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:52,220
to sleep through the
night,

367
00:09:52,220 --> 00:09:53,640
say yes to the walk,

368
00:09:53,640 --> 00:09:55,080
and get my life back.

369
00:09:55,170 --> 00:09:56,530
So take it from me.

370
00:09:56,620 --> 00:09:57,850
Don't spend another year
waiting

371
00:09:57,850 --> 00:09:58,840
for it to settle.

372
00:09:58,880 --> 00:10:00,640
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

373
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:03,090
More than ten thousand
people

374
00:10:03,090 --> 00:10:05,450
with pain after a knee
replacement

375
00:10:05,450 --> 00:10:07,040
have already tried this.

376
00:10:07,420 --> 00:10:09,150
Some had it worse than I
did.

377
00:10:09,270 --> 00:10:10,340
You can get the KenRelief

378
00:10:10,340 --> 00:10:11,780
wrap from their website,

379
00:10:11,780 --> 00:10:13,030
with a discount link

380
00:10:13,030 --> 00:10:14,980
and ninety days to try it.

381
00:10:15,210 --> 00:10:17,130
If it doesn't do anything
for you,

382
00:10:17,130 --> 00:10:18,350
you get your money back

383
00:10:18,350 --> 00:10:19,480
and you keep the wrap.

384
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:20,800
They only release so many

385
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:21,830
at that price.

386
00:10:21,950 --> 00:10:23,190
If it's still there,

387
00:10:23,190 --> 00:10:24,000
get one,

388
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:25,293
and stop the squeeze.

